(Information Access Control Standard) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Standard ID: GRC-AC-2026) Tj
T*
(Version: 1.0) Tj
T*
(Owner: Information Security) Tj
T*
(Effective Date: 2026-01-01) Tj
T*
(Classification: Internal) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Purpose and Scope) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(This standard defines the mandatory controls governing access to production systems and) Tj
T*
(confidential data. It applies to all employees, contractors, and third parties who are) Tj
T*
(granted access to organizational information systems.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2. Definitions) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(An "account" is any credential permitting authentication to a system. A "privileged) Tj
T*
(account" is any account holding administrative rights. "Access review" means a documented) Tj
T*
(confirmation that a person's access remains appropriate for their role.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3. Account Provisioning) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3.1 Access must be approved by the data owner before the account is created.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3.2 Access must be granted on the principle of least privilege. A person must receive only) Tj
T*
(the permissions required to perform their role.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3.3 Shared accounts must not be used for privileged access. Every privileged action must be) Tj
T*
(attributable to one named individual.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(4. Authentication) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(4.1 Multi-factor authentication must be enforced for all remote access to production) Tj
T*
(systems.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(4.2 Passwords must be at least twelve characters in length.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(4.3 Passwords must not be transmitted or stored in plain text.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(5. Access Review and Revocation) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(5.1 Access rights must be reviewed at least quarterly by the data owner.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
